                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "When I first heard about this game and saw footage/screenshots I was really impressed and had high hopes for it. But after development halted and I found out that it was created by only two people my expectations were lowered quite a bit. Not in a bad way, I just went into it thinking 'Oh, it's another indie game that will probably need some polish over time'. After having now played I would say I was about right in my prediction.\n\n[b] GAMEPLAY [/b] - So The Cavern is pretty much an escape the room type of game where you move from room to room (or cave to cave I guess) by solving puzzles. The goal in each room is to unlock the door that leads to the next (or so it seems so far). I haven't finished the game so I'm not sure how big these rooms will get, but so far they are pretty small. \n\n[b] PERFORMANCE [/b] - The games visuals are sharp and I really like the setting. But as for performance, the game does need a bit of work. I have had frame rate jitters (I have a 980 Ti) throughout my play time and objects you interact with can be kind of buggy. I had to start a room over because my lantern got lodged/stuck through a chest. I also noticed that the floor in the game is a lot deeper than my room floor so I was unable to pick up certain objects on the ground (some of which were important). I might try recalibrating SteamVR to see if it fixes it. Lastly, your vision turns black anytime your head goes through a solid object. ANY object, even the lantern you're holding or a twig on a tree. Kind of annoying, but it's not the first game where that happens. Not sure if this is deliberately done in game development or what...\n\n\n[b] PUZZLES [/b] - As for the puzzles, one of the earlier ones was too hard for such and early part of the game in my honest opinion. Maybe 5 or 6 levels down the road sure, but for the second room I thought it was borderline frustrating. I found out that there is a hint system however, which is nice. I haven't played enough to give an overall impression of all of the puzzles but some example are, **[b] minor spoilers inc --> [/b]**, pouring gas into a generator to start it, finding a number code to a chest, using an axe to break through a blocked entryway.\n\nI guess I'm just not a huge fan of escape the room games in general, but yeah. I really like the visuals, environment and story so I kind of wish that puzzles were easier just so I can experience it all in a somewhat relaxing, non-frustrating manner. The treasure hunting aspect of the story reminded me a lot of Uncharted. I'd still recommend checking it out if this sounds like your cup of tea.\n\nI know this review probably sounded kind of negative but I still think there is a really good game here and I am still eager to finish it. It's definitely playable don't get me wrong and I can recommend it. I look forward to seeing it improve in the future.\n\n**Gameplay Vid if anyone cares** --> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vVkPUKxxMes",
